 "title": "Ab0920a and Alternaria brassicicola Pathogenicity and Resistance",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the pathogenicity and resistance of Ab0920a, an isolate of Alternaria brassicicola, a plant pathogen. Ab0920a is an effector of A. brassicicola and has secreted the Bax protein. It is sensitive to various fungicides, including Difenoconazole, Fluopyram, Fluxapyroxad, Hexaconazole, Prochloraz, and Tebuconazole. Alternaria brassicicola elicits the production of Camalexin in broccoli and is a pathogen of Arabidopsis thaliana. The cluster also includes various molecular markers and pathogenicity factors associated with Alternaria, including ATPase and Alt a1. The relationships between these entities highlight the complex interactions between plant pathogens and their hosts, as well as the resistance mechanisms employed by the pathogens.",
